From: mscharged-port
Subject: Forget pipeline configurations recorded by resource discovery
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4

1.0.9 development builds recorded every pipeline configuration that resource
discovery derived from loaded menus and matches: more than 10,000 for a single
match, most of which the game never draws. The port now prepares every known
configuration before the game starts, so these records would add seconds to
each launch. A new configuration version drops them, and configurations are
learned from real draws again. The compiled-pipeline cache is kept, so known
pipelines are not compiled again.

--- a/lib/gx/pipeline.hpp
+++ b/lib/gx/pipeline.hpp
@@ -20,7 +20,7 @@
   uint64_t receiptTag;
 };
 
-constexpr uint32_t GXPipelineConfigVersion = 15;
+constexpr uint32_t GXPipelineConfigVersion = 16;
 struct PipelineConfig {
   uint32_t version = GXPipelineConfigVersion;
   uint32_t msaaSamples = 1; // deprecated
